PS5 USB-C DP: off by default, opt in with usbc_dp.enable=1

Programming the front USB-C port's DisplayPort policy (PR #57) can reset a device on
that port, e.g. a boot drive there. Slip's hdmi-usbc-test branch makes it opt-in for
the same reason. USB-C displays and PSVR2: add usbc_dp.enable=1 to cmdline.txt.
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/usbc_dp.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/usbc_dp.c
@@ -24,9 +24,14 @@
  * real HPD and DRM detection/modesetting still control the video stream.
  * enable=0 keeps the port controller policy untouched for diagnostics.
  */
-static bool enable = true;
+/*
+ * Off by default programming the port's DP
+ * policy can reset a device on the front USB-C port, e.g. a boot drive there. USB-C
+ * displays and PSVR2: usbc_dp.enable=1 in cmdline.txt.
+ */
+static bool enable;
 module_param(enable, bool, 0444);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable, "Prepare FAT USB-C DP policy automatically: Sony/Genesys RAM allowlist and NORMAL mode (default: on; 0 leaves policy unchanged)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(enable, "Prepare FAT USB-C DP policy (Sony/Genesys RAM allowlist and NORMAL mode) for USB-C displays/PSVR2 (default: off; it can reset a device on the front USB-C port)");
 
 static unsigned int dp_lanes = 4;
 module_param(dp_lanes, uint, 0444);
